<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28994" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mīca</span></b> , ae, f.
		root smic-; Gr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σμικρός</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μικρός</span>; cf. micula; O. Germ. smahan, to
			belittle, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a crumb, little bit, morsel, grain</i> (<b>poet.</b> and in post-Aug. prose). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mica panis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Petr. 42</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">auri,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lucr.
					1, 839</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">marmoris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					33, 4, 21, § 68</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">salis,</span>”
				<i>a grain of salt</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					22, 14, 16, § 37</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">amomi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					12, 18, 41, § 83</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">saliens (i. e. salis) mica,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 3, 23, 12</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tus in micas friatur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					12, 14, 32, § 65</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">de micis puerorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Marc. 7, 28</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>A small diningroom</i>, <i><span class="en">Mart. 2,
				59, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sen. Ep. 51,
			12</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			In gen., <i>a little bit, a grain</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nulla in tam magno est corpore mica salis,</span>”
				<i>a grain of sense</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cat.
					86, 3</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
